cuisine, miodownik or stefanka is a type of layer cake flavoured with honey, similar to cakes in other Slavic cuisines such as the Russian medovik and Czech medovnik. It is broadly considered a type of piernik, meaning a sweet and/or spiced confectionery good. The recipe for miodownik originates from Galicia (Southeastern Poland) and Central Poland."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-miodownik"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miodownik"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine"],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Honey","ingredient/honey"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Tori Avey: Jewish Recipes","ref":"site/toriavey-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"toriavey.com","note":"Tori Avey's Jewish recipe index, often paired with notes on each dish's history.","url":"https://toriavey.com/jewish-recipes/","suggested":true},{"name":"The Nosher (My Jewish Learning)","ref":"site/myjewishlearning-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"myjewishlearning.com","note":"Recipe section of the nonprofit My Jewish Learning, covering Ashkenazi, Sephardi and Mizrahi home cooking and holiday food.","url":"https://www.myjewishlearning.com/recipes/","suggested":true},{"name":"Polonist","ref":"site/polonist-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polonist.com","note":"Polish recipes and food culture from a Polish-born writer living abroad.","url":"https://www.polonist.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Polish Your Kitchen","ref":"site/polishyourkitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polishyourkitchen.com","note":"Long-running blog of traditional Polish home recipes.","url":"https://polishyourkitchen.com","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Jewish cuisine","links":[["Appetizing store","dish/appetizing-store"],["Bagel","dish/bagel"],["Brent's Deli","dish/brent-s